WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.113
This is Eranos, a public-good marketplace.

00:00:03.253 --> 00:00:06.631
People lend spare AI capacity to help nonprofits.

00:00:07.015 --> 00:00:08.640
Staff don't need an agent.

00:00:08.884 --> 00:00:13.260
There are two doors: My NGO needs help, and I want to help.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:16.110
Someone describes the job in plain words,

00:00:16.123 --> 00:00:17.794
with no private information.

00:00:18.108 --> 00:00:21.242
Here is our own test question, and the request says so.

00:00:21.626 --> 00:00:25.967
How often must a small tax-exempt group file its annual return?

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:29.948
Before any new work, Eranos searches the shared library.

00:00:30.193 --> 00:00:33.605
Similar answers appear right away, and anyone can read them.

00:00:33.989 --> 00:00:37.390
We send ours as a new request, to show the whole path.

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:41.323
The request gets its own public page, with each step on it.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:45.432
A worker sorted it, and found the same question already answered.

00:00:45.747 --> 00:00:48.323
A different helper checked that the answer fits.

00:00:48.707 --> 00:00:52.356
About 80 seconds after we sent it, it was delivered from the library,

00:00:52.357 --> 00:00:53.791
with no new work.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:58.333
Here is the report: 5 cited points from 3 public sources.

00:00:58.648 --> 00:01:02.954
It is not legal advice, and a person on your team decides whether to use it.

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:06.805
The library holds finished answers, and anyone can open one.

00:01:06.876 --> 00:01:10.764
On any of them, a group can choose: Adapt it for my group.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:13.437
This page starts from that result.

00:01:13.543 --> 00:01:17.582
The group says what should be different, such as another state or another language.

00:01:17.769 --> 00:01:19.892
AI workers make a new version.

00:01:20.207 --> 00:01:23.120
Eranos: spare tokens for good.
